356: four-dimensional fixed-surface signature
357: identity. With weights \(+1,-1\), its
358: normal-link contribution is
359: \[
360:  \frac1{24}\int_{S_{\rm c}\cup(-S_{\rm r})}
361:             \{p_1(TS)-3b^2\}=-\frac{a^2}{4}.           \tag{IE.8}
362: \]
363: There are exactly \(N\) E doubles: the actual
364: scalar period shifts the primitive chain by
365: \(N\), and the collision-boundary source
366: loop fixes these labels.
367: 
368: ## IE.4. Finite stabilizers and the actual Stokes identity
369: 
370: Remove invariant normal tubes of every fixed
371: component from \(W_{\rm rel}\). The physical
372: circle is locally free on the complement.
373: Its quotient is a compact oriented
374: seven-dimensional orbifold \(Z\), carrying
375: the actual orbifold Euler line with class \(x\).
376: 
377: A slice with stabilizer \(\mu_d\) gives a
378: finite chart \(\widetilde U/\mu_d\). Average
379: metrics, partitions of unity and connections
380: over \(\mu_d\) and over the physical circle.
381: Normalize the connection by
382: \(\alpha(\delta)=1\). Its curvature represents
383: the same physical \(x\) on every chart. The
384: actual tangent splitting is
385: \[
386:  TW_{\rm rel}|_{\rm locally\ free}
387:                     \cong\pi^*TZ\oplus\mathbb R_\delta .      \tag{IE.9}
388: \]
389: Choose its connection to match the actual
390: boundary tangent connections after a collar
391: interpolation. The basic Chern--Weil form
392: \[
393:                       \Omega=\frac{4x^3-p_1(TZ)x}{24}         \tag{IE.10}
394: \]
395: is closed. Integrate each finite chart as
396: \(d^{-1}\int_{\widetilde U}\). Ordinary Stokes
397: on the finite covers and their averaged
398: partition of unity cancels every interior
399: face with exactly these multiplicities.
400: The finite-isotropy strata are not boundary
401: faces. Consequently
402: \(\int_{\partial Z}\Omega=0\).
403: 
404: On a fixed normal link, (IE.9) restricts
405: to the fixed tangent and weighted normal
406: bundles. Its equivariant Thom denominator
407: is \(\prod_i(x_i+w_i u)\). The finite
408: chart integral, equivalently the weighted
409: projective power map, gives
410: \(1/\prod_iw_i\), with every negative
411: normal conjugation's orientation sign.
412: Thus its actual contribution is (IE.16), proved below.
413: The compact interior/H values and (IE.8)
414: are exactly the terms in this Stokes
415: identity, including finite stabilizers.
416: No spin structure on this comparison
417: bordism or eight-dimensional signature
418: formula is used.
419: 
420: ## IE.5. Outer boundary and Jin conventions
421: 
422: Orient \(W_{\rm c}\) complexly and the
423: reference piece oppositely. Define
424: \(\delta\wedge\operatorname{or}(Z)
425: =\operatorname{or}(W_{\rm rel})\).
426: Near the outer parameter boundary,
427: \[
428:  \operatorname{or}(W)
429:  =\delta\wedge\operatorname{or}(Y)
430:                   \wedge d\rho\wedge d\theta .
431: \]
432: Since \(\dim Y=5\), its quotient boundary
433: orientation is
434: \[
435:                          -\operatorname{or}(Y)\wedge d\theta.       \tag{IE.11}
436: \]
437: At an inner fixed-normal boundary the
438: minus sign from removing the normal disc
439: and the minus sign from quotienting an
440: oriented boundary by the odd-dimensional
441: orbit cancel. Its orientation is the
442: positive complex-normal link convention
443: of (IE.16). Therefore Stokes gives
444: \[
445:                  A_{\rm physical,difference}
446:                           =\sum_F\mathcal R(F).          \tag{IE.12}
447: \]
448: 
449: Jin identifies \((z,0)\sim(f(z),1)\).
450: The positive physical family with return
451: \(f\) has the inverse parameter marking.
452: The map to the Jin six-manifold reverses
453: that circle and preserves the physical
454: Euler line. Hence
455: \[
456:                   A_{\rm Jin,difference}
457:                            =-\sum_F\mathcal R(F).         \tag{IE.13}
458: \]
459: The common conifold replacement in IE.2
460: uses the same transported positive
461: meridian, so adds no line or orientation
462: change.
463: 
